The fresh oracle pool happened to fail all three 48-vertex instances, so the script stopped at `easy`. I’m now applying the non-LLM gate to that exact preset; if the cheap restart attack solves it, the README will explicitly reject easy and retain 108 as the first gate-clean shipping level, while preserving the script’s honest transcript.
